.TH KRONEIN-WALLET "1" "September 2026" "kronein-wallet v31.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kronein-wallet \- manual page for kronein-wallet v31.1.0
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kronein-wallet
[\fI\,options\/\fR] \fI\,<command>\/\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Kronein Core kronein\-wallet utility version v31.1.0
.PP
kronein\-wallet is an offline tool for creating and interacting with Kronein Core wallet files.
.PP
By default kronein\-wallet will act on wallets in the default mainnet wallet directory in the datadir.
.PP
To change the target wallet, use the \fB\-datadir\fR, \fB\-wallet\fR and (test)chain selection arguments.
.SH OPTIONS
.HP
\fB\-datadir=\fR<dir>
.IP
Specify data directory
.HP
\fB\-dumpfile=\fR<file name>
.IP
When used with 'dump', writes out the records to this file. When used
with 'createfromdump', loads the records into a new wallet.
.HP
\fB\-help\fR
.IP
Print this help message and exit (also \fB\-h\fR or \-?)
.HP
\fB\-version\fR
.IP
Print version and exit
.HP
\fB\-wallet=\fR<wallet\-name>
.IP
Specify wallet name
.PP
Debugging/Testing options:
.HP
\fB\-debug=\fR<category>
.IP
Output debugging information (default: 0).
.HP
\fB\-printtoconsole\fR
.IP
Send trace/debug info to console (default: 1 when no \fB\-debug\fR is true, 0
otherwise).
.PP
Chain selection options:
.HP
\fB\-chain=\fR<chain>
.IP
Use the chain <chain> (default: main). Allowed values: main, testnet4,
signet, regtest
.HP
\fB\-signet\fR
.IP
Use the signet chain. Equivalent to \fB\-chain\fR=\fI\,signet\/\fR. Note that the network
is defined by the \fB\-signetchallenge\fR parameter
.HP
\fB\-signetchallenge\fR
.IP
Blocks must provide a Taproot witness satisfying this P2TR scriptPubKey
(only for signet networks; defaults to the project Signet
challenge)
.HP
\fB\-signetseednode\fR
.IP
Specify a seed node for the signet network, in the hostname[:port]
format, e.g. sig.net:1234 (may be used multiple times)
.HP
\fB\-testnet4\fR
.IP
Use the testnet4 chain. Equivalent to \fB\-chain\fR=\fI\,testnet4\/\fR.
.PP
Commands:
.IP
create
.IP
Create a new descriptor wallet file
.IP
createfromdump
.IP
Create new wallet file from dumped records
.IP
dump
.IP
Print out all of the wallet key\-value records
.IP
info
.IP
Get wallet info
